d by her Chinese grandmother  because her mother passed away when she  was four and you know just really  connected with the story with the  relationship between Billy and her  grandmother and  said you know I got to do this and she  sent an audition tape in and when I saw  the audition tape I was blown away I  just didn't know that she had that in  her she's really terrific I'm curious  when you brought the idea of this film  to sort of Hollywood Finance ears how  they reacted to it oh they were like  take all the money  subtitled all Asian cats where's my  check interested at least yes they were  interested in the premise  you know they felt like oh this ruse  this facade it's kind of screwball let's  take that and let's run with it let's go  more screwball let's go broader let's  make this my big fat Chinese wedding  let's put a white character in they  wanted a white character him that was  actually a Chinese investor he said you  know if we're gonna bring this film to  Chinese audiences the thing that's gonna  be entertaining for them to watch is  somebody who's American I said well  Billy's American he said no no no like a  real American real American right  exactly like a white guy that she brings  home doesn't understand the culture and  well laugh at the fact that he can't use  chopsticks like that's not the story so  glad you were able to hold on to your  vision for this film because it's a  beautiful film and it's a wonderful film  for people who are trying to understand  the way others around the world may  think of tradition and duty and it's  just it's also it's a universal film too  because I think everybody can see their  own family and that's why the response  has been so good Lulu Wong thank you  very much thank you that's what the film  we appreciate your visit here the  farewell is in theaters nationwide now
 

